# Everything the packaged .vsix does not need at runtime.

.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
.github/**
.git/**
.gitignore
.hirayacoder/**

# Local scratch space. `.gitignore` covers it for git, and a `.vscodeignore` file does
# NOT inherit those rules — so this was shipping inside the .vsix while being invisible
# to `git status`: real evaluation transcripts, complete with the absolute paths of the
# machine they were recorded on. Anything untracked is more likely to be private, not
# less, so it is excluded first and explicitly.
.ignore/**

# Agent tooling for people working on this repo, not for people installing it.
.claude/**

# The benchmark corpus and its results. Development-only, in the same way `tools/**`
# below is — nothing under `app/` reads either.
benchmarks/**

# Source-of-truth material that isn't shipped code.
# NOTE: setup/prompts/** is deliberately NOT excluded — promptLoader.js reads the
# model-facing prompts from there at runtime. Excluding them would silently drop the
# extension onto its embedded fallback prompts in production. Only the build spec,
# which is for humans, is left out.
# Every top-level setup document is for humans building the project, not for the
# packaged extension. A pattern rather than a list, because the previous version named
# two files individually and the third one silently shipped.
setup/*.md
security/**
test/**
builds/**
doc/**

# Everything installed, without exception.
#
# This extension has no runtime dependencies and never has had: `dependencies` is `{}`,
# and everything under `node_modules` is build and test tooling. vsce prunes to the
# production tree by itself, which is why this line was not needed until something put
# packages there that package.json had never asked for — the v0.5.3 model round ran
# `npm install` at the workspace root, because a command could not run anywhere else,
# and the next build went from 0.37 MB to 22.69 MB with 3,749 files of React tooling
# inside it.
#
# The prune is the fix; this is the guarantee. IF A RUNTIME DEPENDENCY IS EVER ADDED,
# this line has to go, or the shipped extension will be missing it.
node_modules/**

# Tooling config
eslint.config.js
scripts/**
# The live-model benchmark harness. Development-only: nothing under app/ requires it,
# and it was shipping in the .vsix because only source *folders* were excluded.
tools/**
**/*.map
**/tsconfig.json
**/jsconfig.json
.mocharc*

# Keep: README.md, CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE, package.json, app/**, docs/assets/icon-128.png
docs/assets/**
!docs/assets/icon-128.png
!docs/assets/icon-16.png
# The activity bar glyph. Referenced by `contributes.viewsContainers`, so leaving it out
# ships an extension whose sidebar icon is a blank square.
!docs/assets/activity-bar.svg
